## 2. Formal statement and assumptions (C1)

Fix odd `p>=3`. For nonempty `w=(eps_0..eps_{m-1})`, `eps_0=1`, `k=sum eps`:

- `B_w=sum_{j:eps_j=1} 2^j p^{sum_{t>j}eps_t}`, `D=2^m-p^k`, `A=|D|`, `b=sign(D)`.
- Formal composition: `H_w(x)=(p^k x+bB_w)/2^m` as rationals (verified on 2000 random words).
- Formal positive candidate `q(w)=B_w/A` (since `x=bB_w/D=B_w/|D|`).
- For rotation `r` (length `m`, same `k`; may start with 0), `B_r` by same formula.
- `h_b(r)` = unique `h in {1..2^m}` with `h==-bB_r(p^k)^{-1} mod 2^m` (`0`→`2^m`).

C1: for every primitive `w` (aperiodic; not `u^t`, `t>1`), if for every cyclic rotation `r`, `q(r)=B_r/A >= h_b(r)` (i.e. `B_r>=A h_b(r)` as integers), then `A|B_w`.

## 3. Definition validation

- `D!=0`: `2^m` vs odd `p^k` cannot be equal (unique factorization). Checked all `m<25`.
- `B_w>0`: `k>=1` (first bit 1), sum has positive term.
- `A` odd, `gcd(2^m,A)=1`, `gcd(p,A)=1` (since `A==2^m mod p !=0`).
- `b=sign(D)` is the positive branch: `B>0` gives `x=bB/D>0` iff `b=sign(D)`.
- `h` residue: verified for all `2^m` words, `m<=8`, `p=3,5`, both `b`, that starting from `h` and applying actual `H_{p,b}` reproduces the word for `m` steps. Parity matches: `B==e0 mod 2`, `-b==1 mod 2`, `p^k` odd, so `h==e0 mod 2`. `h==2^m` occurs only when `2^m|B`, hence `B` even and first bit 0 — consistent.
- `B` under rotation: proved and machine-checked (all words `m<=11`, `p=3,5,7`) that with `D=2^m-p^k`, adjacent left rotation satisfies `B'=B/2` if `e0=0` (then `B` even), `B'=(pB+D)/2` if `e0=1` (then `pB+D` even as odd+odd). No divisibility assumed: parity follows from `B==e0 mod 2` and `D` odd. After `m` steps returns to `B`.
- Primitive convention: primitive = aperiodic; then `m` rotations distinct. C1 restricts to primitive, but scan finds zero non-integral survivors even among non-primitive rows through 22.
- Key congruence: `p^k==2^m-bA==-bA mod 2^m`, so `-b(p^k)^{-1}==A^{-1} mod 2^m`; hence `h==BA^{-1}==q mod 2^m` as 2-adic integers (odd denominator). So integer `q` always satisfies `q>=h` (write `q=h+s2^m`, `s>=0` since `q>=1`, `h<=2^m`, difference a multiple of `2^m`).

