- `n_r>=0` iff `B_r/A>=h_b(r)/2^m`. Since `2^m>=1`, C1 premise `B_r>=A h_b(r)` implies `n_r>=0`, but converse is false and much weaker. Separation example `p=3,m=4,w=(1,1,0,0)`, `A=7`: all `n_r` are `59,85,236,118>=0` while all `B_r-Ah_r` are `-16,-80,-64,-32<0`.
